    {
      "ordinal": 9,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "4.2",
      "title": "Visor",
      "body": "Visors must be made of metal grill or plates, concealed under chainmail.\n\nChainmail must be properly attached to the visor with metal, leather or fabric thread.\n\nVisors must not be too long or too short and respect the proportions of historical sources.\n\nNasal helmet visor bottom line must end between nose and chin.\n\nThe fixation system must be reproduced as per historical sources (“spoon” or “cross”).\n\nIt is allowed to add a metal plate to protect the throat. Such a plate must be strong enough to endure\n\nfull contact fight and must be concealed under the Aventail.",
      "page_from": 6,
      "page_to": 6,
      "stable_key": "nasals-and-breteches:4.2",
      "parent_key": "nasals-and-breteches:4",
      "review_status": "extracted",
